# Teach the VoiceChat converters to read a Q8_0 source container.
# 
# The published `llamacpp/` folder in hoidhxd/NVIDIA-NemotronLabs-VoiceChat-11B-GGUF
# holds only the Q4_0 split, so a Q8_0 set has to be made from the Q8_0 container
# with these same three converters. They do not read one as shipped:
# 
#   vc_gguf.GGUFSource.f32() has a dequantizer for Q4_0 and none for Q8_0, so it
#   exits with "cannot read Q8_0 as float" the first time the perception or TTS
#   converter needs a quantized tensor as a float — which both do, because a few
#   tensors are added rather than multiplied and ggml wants those dense.
# 
# Nothing about the copy path changes: quantized tensors still move block for
# block and stay bit-identical, Q8_0 in, Q8_0 out. Only the handful of tensors
# that were already being dequantized in the Q4_0 flow are affected.
# 
# Three changes:
# 
#   1. vc_gguf.dequant_q8_0, and the f32() branch that calls it. Q8_0 is 32
#      elements per block, an f16 scale then 32 signed bytes.
#   2. The same branch in convert_voicechat_to_nemotron_h.py, which carries its
#      own reader. In practice it should never fire: the tensors that converter
#      reads as float are all rank-1 and both published quantizations keep those
#      at F16 on purpose. It is there so a hand-rolled requantization that broke
#      that rule fails softly rather than at the last block.
#   3. general.file_type follows the source instead of being hardcoded Q4_0.
#      Metadata only, but it is in every log line that names the file.
# 
# Against sansamour/llama-voicechat.cpp @ f45001fc (branch voicechat).

--- a/tools/voicechat/vc_gguf.py	2026-08-29 12:19:35.584011100 +0500
